A||||10||Richard Parnell||Wrecked my Fiero last night||||8||
Z||000000||Richard Parnell||04-06-2001||12:34 PM||||Last night on my way home I was passing some cars and ran into some one in front of me turning left.  It was wet I didn't see her signaling and the road was wet.  My fault, dumb move.  The collision ripped the headlights off, tore the left side of the hood halfway up the drivers' side , split the front fascia and busted up the left front fender. In addition it looks like it shoved the hood up against the windshield.  Luckily it didn't crack the windshield.  No one hurt, the lady was cool about it, she and I were both in shock. The cops were cool and best of all I wasn't drunk as I would have been 6 months ago. I could see it coming but my wheels were locked. I slid right up under the rear side of her Geo.  I think all it did was rip the tailpipe off her car.  I'm going to have to take the day off and assess if the car is worth fixing.  I'm sick, I just got the 350 in it a couple of months ago and had everything working well.  There's and abondoned 87 SC like mine up the road.  I'm going to have to bribe a tow truck to bring it here as abandoned cars are not supposed to be towed by anyone other than the state here.  Sh*t!!!||||reg||8
Z||000001||turbo86se||04-06-2001||01:02 PM||||Sorry to hear about your accident. Sounds to me it's mainly cosmetic? If you need a fender or some headlight doors, I'll donate them!||||reg||1
Z||000002||KRMFiero||04-06-2001||02:20 PM||||I hope you get it fixed soon, you have a real nice car||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfixit58||04-06-2001||02:23 PM||||Oh, Dude. sorry to hear that. keep us posted.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||9
Z||000004||Richard Parnell||04-06-2001||02:58 PM||||I can get everything except the front fascia right away.  I may need those headlight doors too.  I'll pay for shipping of the headlite doors.  Does anyone have the fascia?||||reg||9
Z||000005||Richard Parnell||04-06-2001||08:09 PM||||Well, got the front fascia, hood and left front fender off.  Found everything (I hope) I need at the local boneyard.  Man, everything came of easy except when it came to the last two fasteners for the fender by the bottom of the door, I had to drill out the rivets for the molding under the door and then the last two fasteners for the fender turned out to be rivets also.  I don't know how I'm going to fasten the one that I can't get to from the back.  The wall that holds the headlight on the driver side is bent in , hope I can get it straight enough to align the headlight.  Man oh man what a hassle.  So much for doing the suspension any time soon.  My poor gold beauty will be multicolored for a while.  I feel really down, first my wife of 32 years decides to leave (divorce went through 2 weeks ago), have to sell my house here at Sunset beach and now this.  I don't even feel like getting up in the morning sometimes.||||reg||9
Z||000006||Kelvin Vivian||04-06-2001||08:21 PM||||Well when it's tough, it's best to just focus on one thing at a time.  Sad to hear that the gold beauty is busted, hopefully it is just cosmetic, and sounds like you have most of the necessary parts to fix her up.<P>Give it time...||||reg||9
Z||000007||hugh||04-06-2001||09:49 PM||||Richard,2 things are important.One is you weren't hurt and two,things will get better.||||reg||1
Z||000008||fyerstarter||04-06-2001||09:59 PM||||Sorry to hear that. I wrecked my Fiero the exact same way the first week that I had it. Cept I swerved around the car and drove through a tennis court :\<P>But she's all fixed now. These cars take a remarkable beating with only some cosmetic damage. Things can only look up from here  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000009||Jake_Dragon||04-06-2001||10:59 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B>Last night on my way home I was passing some cars and ran into some one in front of me turning left. It was wet I didn't see her signaling and the road was wet. I could see it coming but my wheels were locked.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I had my front wheels lock in the same way. Took out a hedge and hit a tree. I kept my head and pumped the breaks enough to steer around a bus.<BR>I hope you get it back on the road soon! Stick with it and you will be waxing her before you know it.<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://home1.gte.net/rebel33/fiero.jpg"> ||||reg||14
Z||000010||Richard Parnell||04-08-2001||05:37 AM||||Thanks guys,  I was hoping to have it all back together this weekend but having problems getting the parts from the boneyard to here. Probably will have to take sometime off or rent a car.||||reg||1
